.TH OOBED 8 2026-10-19 "Peios installer 0.1.13"
.SH NAME
oobed \- Peios first-boot setup service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oobed
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-browser
.I path
.RB | \-\-no-browser ]
.RB [ \-\-dry-run
.RB [ \-\-net-status
.IR file ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oobed
creates the first administrator account, records the machine name, and
applies a pending manual wired-network setting.
It serves the Message Surface Interaction Protocol (MSIP) conversation to
.BR oobe-tui (1)
and, when installed,
.BR oobe-gxwi (1).
Both frontends share the same conversation.
.PP
The network page reads
.B net status
and refreshes when requested.
A manual address, gateway, and name servers are saved until the final apply
step, after account creation and machine naming.
The resulting profile and interface rule belong to the network service.
Wireless-network joining is not provided by this flow.
.PP
Account names are trimmed and checked against local account-store rules.
Passwords must be nonempty, match, and contain no carriage return or
line feed.
Unicode characters, spaces, and tabs are preserved.
Reserved group names and
.B peios-oobe-setup
are rejected as account names.
The machine name must be one label of at most 63 letters, digits, and
hyphens, without a leading or trailing hyphen, and cannot be
.BR localhost .
.PP
Browser setup uses the GXWI overlay.
Before accepting clients, the daemon creates or reuses the passwordless
account
.B peios-oobe-setup
and admits it to the intended socket descriptor.
It then sets GXWI's overlay values.
Successful setup removes the overlay, the temporary account and its home,
and the setup service definitions.
Unfinished setup retains the definitions for another boot.
.PP
The console's welcome page reports the browser address and certificate
fingerprint when available.
It reads
.I /var/state/gxwi/certificate.sha256
and refreshes the page every 3 seconds.
Verify the fingerprint through a trusted console before entering browser
credentials.
The browser page is not itself a source of certificate trust.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Listen on PATH instead of
.IR /run/oobed.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-browser " PATH"
The program GXWI runs to draw setup in a browser. The default is
.IR /bin/oobe-gxwi ;
if it is not installed, setup is on the console only.
.TP
.B \-\-no-browser
Setup on the console only.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Exercise the setup conversation without changing the machine. No account is
created and no overlay is set, so a browser program is pointed at the socket
by hand.
.TP
.BI \-\-net-status " FILE"
With
.BR \-\-dry-run ,
take FILE to be what
.B net status
prints, read afresh each time the network page asks. Without it, a dry run
cannot say anything of the network.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Show the program version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The daemon writes the machine name, network profiles, and rules under
.BR Machine\eSystem\eNetwork ,
and overlay values under
.BR Machine\eSoftware\eGXWI .
It removes the
.B oobed
and
.B oobe-tui
service definitions after successful setup.
The registry interfaces of those owning components define their value
semantics.
.SH SECURITY
The daemon runs as SYSTEM.
Its intended socket descriptor admits SYSTEM, Administrators, and the
temporary browser account when browser setup is offered.
Failure to apply that descriptor produces a warning and leaves inherited
access in effect.
.PP
The temporary account has no password and no groups.
Any sign-in mechanism accepting passwordless accounts can accept it while
it exists.
The browser overlay is available without normal sign-in; keep the machine
on a trusted network until setup finishes.
.PP
Passwords are sent to
.B lps
over standard input rather than process arguments and are not written to
the MSIP log.
.PP
Startup removes the supplied socket path before binding, including in
dry-run mode.
Use a new, protected directory for rehearsal sockets.
Dry-run does not create accounts or configure a browser overlay.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help, version, or successful setup completion.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.TP
.B 101
An unrecoverable listener or server error caused a Rust panic.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
Service-manager socket that receives readiness after setup has bound its
socket and prepared browser access.
.TP
.B PATH
Used to locate account, network, registry, and security tools.
Run the privileged daemon with a trusted executable search path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/oobed.sock
Default MSIP socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lps (1),
.BR net (1),
.BR oobe-tui (1),
.BR reg (1)
